      "knowledge_point_id": "52e11164-1929-594d-9f9e-460f6469421d",
      "knowledge_point": "Graphing a Stretched Negative Reciprocal Function",
      "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of $y=-\\frac{3}{4x}?$",
      "worked_solution": "To plot $y=-\\frac{3}{4x},$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=-\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13831126/assets/d5d93e12275c683e0a56f0ec9a0c99540a7774879cd0f8fa69151ddba68a44fa.png)\n\n- Stretch the result by a scale factor of $\\frac{3}{4}$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=-\\frac{3}{4x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13831126/assets/76d779da22082439eb40586ddbeb325368b1f49f15fef3158ebaa0eee90f4d84.png)",
